// Exports { signup, config }.
//
// WHY THIS SHAPE
// Draft 1 ("throw everything at every field") produced 3932 differences but covered only
// 2 of the 7 reachable behaviour changes. Reason, from fuzz/run.js's own rule: an input only
// counts as exercising a change when EVERY OTHER field is valid under zod 3, and a nine-field
// random object is broken in several places at once. So this file is built the other way round:
//
//     sample = a deliberately boring, zod-3-valid BASE object
//            + a stress value in (usually) exactly ONE field
//
